- op: discuss  # 2fdb
  at: '2026-06-02T06:13:52Z'  # 2fdb
  by: agent  # 2fdb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2fdb
  clock: 4  # 2fdb
  nonce: 2fdb  # 2fdb
  message: "Pass-27 INV-kurup new face — six sibling hashed-identifier fields use four distinct prefix conventions plus one absent-field convention.\n\nPass-27 surveyed every top-level identifier-bearing field that carries a content-addressed (hash-based) value. Results:\n\n| Field | Format | Sample |\n|---|---|---|\n| node.stable_id | `sha256:<16hex>` (1 colon) | `sha256:fc4f52d59df5d3a5` |\n| edge.id | `edge:sha256:<16hex>` (2 colons) | `edge:sha256:17ae7e43bd3ca98c` |\n| edge.edge_key | `edgekey:sha256:<16hex>` (2 colons) | `edgekey:sha256:4ca7645b4389a13d` |\n| feature.id | `sha256:<16hex>` (1 colon) | `sha256:71d09c5dcdf3a4a8` |\n| usage_context.id | `usage:sha256:<16hex>` (2 colons) | `usage:sha256:20d859135eb74337` |\n| entrypoint.id | **(field absent)** | — |\n\nSix sibling \"stable hashed identifier of this record\" fields, three concrete prefix conventions (`sha256:`, `<recordkind>:sha256:`, `usage:sha256:`) plus the entrypoint exception of having no id field at all. Consumers writing dedup/cross-ref code must learn which surface uses which convention.\n\nQuantitative:\n- 109915 edges all use `edge:sha256:<16hex>` for id (100%)\n- 109915 edges all use `edgekey:sha256:<16hex>` for edge_key (100%)\n- 34117 nodes use `sha256:<16hex>` for stable_id (99.6% — 136 None per pass-26 F26.10 / F27.10 below)\n- 16 features all use bare `sha256:<16hex>` for id\n- 8 usage_contexts all use `usage:sha256:<16hex>`\n- 104 entrypoints have no id field at all (0/104)\n\nINV-kurup's existing statement covers \"raw hex, bare names, or extra-colon variants\" abstractly; this is a clean per-field tabulation showing the canonical-hashed-id family alone has four conventions. The fix path could be either schema-level (canonicalize all to `<record>:sha256:<16hex>`) or document-only (declare each surface's convention in spec). Note: edge.edge_key and edge.id are TWO hashed-ids on the same edge record — pass-22's earlier WI-niboh observation (edge.id vs edge.edge_key naming-convention divergence from Symbol's id/stable_id pair) is now refined: not just naming-axis-uniformity but also prefix-convention divergence (edge.id uses `edge:` while edge.edge_key uses `edgekey:`).\n\nProbe artifact: /tmp/pass27_probe2.py + /tmp/pass27_probe5.py / outputs at /tmp/pass27_output[2,5].log.\n\nNo status change; pass-27 just enriches the quantitative face."  # 2fdb
- op: discuss  # 4c0e
  at: '2026-06-02T17:32:57Z'  # 4c0e
  by: agent  # 4c0e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 4c0e
  clock: 5  # 4c0e
  nonce: 4c0e  # 4c0e
  message: "Pass-35 F35.A1 — doc/config analyzer id-format violations: 3 distinct sub-mechanisms (4321 total when --include-docs activates these writers).\n\nINV-kurup scope is \"META: Identifier-bearing fields emit non-canonical formats from several emission sites.\" Pass-35 finds doc/config analyzers (markdown + gitignore) constitute a NEW emission-site category at significant scale — gated behind `--include-docs` so they don't fire in default self-analysis, but when activated produce 4321 Symbol.id + Symbol.stable_id format violations.\n\nSubstrate `/tmp/p35_docs.json` (hypergumbo run --include-docs) validation_report breakdown:\n\n**Mechanism 1 — gitignore-pattern reuses Symbol.id as Symbol.stable_id (2667 cases).** Symbol.stable_id violations on records like:\n```\ngitignore:.ci/.gitignore:2-2:full-suite.log:pattern\ngitignore:.ci/.gitignore:5-5:.smart-test.lock:pattern\ngitignore:.ci/.gitignore:6-6:.smart-test.lock.pid:pattern\n```\nValidator message: `composite_no_sha_prefix (colon_count=4). Use a make_*_stable_id factory from analyze/base.py (or _short_sha256 directly) rather than constructing stable_ids with f-strings or raw hashlib.sha256(...).hexdigest().` The gitignore analyzer is writing the literal Symbol.id string AS the stable_id, not the sha256-hash form. ADR-0034's id-construction discipline applies; the gitignore-pattern emitter at the analyzer level bypasses `make_typed_stable_id`.\n\n**Mechanism 2 — markdown section ID includes section-title literal colons (825 + 825 cases).** Symbol.id and Symbol.stable_id violations on records like:\n```\nmarkdown:AGENTS.md:62-63:Priority Queues::section\nmarkdown:AGENTS.md:65-66:BROAD Mode Priority Queue::section\nmarkdown:AGENTS.md:68-69:DEEP Mode Priority Queue::section\n```\nValidator message: `double_colon_separator (INV-sadiv). Use make_symbol_id(...) from analyze/base.py rather than constructing IDs with f-strings.` The section title contains a `:` which gets concatenated literally → 5 colons total. The markdown analyzer needs name-segment sanitization.\n\n**Mechanism 3 — markdown code_block uses 'code' literal as span segment (584 cases).** Symbol.id violations on records where span position has the literal word `code` instead of `start-end` line range:\nValidator message: `malformed_span_segment ('code'). Use make_symbol_id(...) from analyze/base.py...`. The code_block emitter constructs IDs as `markdown:file.md:code:NAME:code_block` instead of `markdown:file.md:start-end:NAME:code_block`.\n\n**Cross-reference with closure campaign.** The INV-sugat closure campaign (Phase 5) shipped ADR-0034 + the `make_symbol_id` / `make_typed_stable_id` factories AND migrated 10 mainstream code analyzers. Doc/config analyzers (markdown, gitignore, plus likely toml/yaml/json analyzers that ship config-kind nodes — pass-35 didn't sweep beyond markdown + gitignore) were NOT migrated. The mainstream-code-analyzer Phase 6 sweep closed Symbol.id violations on the default substrate but doc/config code-paths use their own pre-factory ID-construction.\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** Mirror Phase 6's mainstream-analyzer sweep on the doc/config analyzer set:\n- markdown analyzer: switch to `make_symbol_id` for all 3 sub-mechanisms; sanitize name segment to escape colons; replace 'code' literal with `start-end` line span\n- gitignore analyzer: switch to `make_*_stable_id` factory call instead of reusing Symbol.id\n- audit toml/yaml/json/markdown-link analyzers for parallel violations (pass-35 didn't sweep these)\n\nDirection is concretely actionable — 3 sub-mechanisms × 2 analyzers = 6 targeted code changes likely close all 4321 violations.\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p35_docs.json` (substrate); `/tmp/p35_probeA.py` + `/tmp/p35_outputA.log` (violation classification). No status change."  # 4c0e
